# The runtime bundle must check out LF everywhere: schema/templates are read
# byte-wise (a stray \r must not become part of a value), and two installs are
# compared by their bytes — the same bundle must check out identical on every OS.
#
# This lives INSIDE the bundle on purpose. Copying .grovespec/ into a project
# carries the rule along, so the install never has to edit — or overwrite — that
# project's own root .gitattributes. A nested file also outranks any root rule
# (gitattributes(5): the closer directory wins), so a project-wide `eol=crlf`
# can't break the runtime.
* text eol=lf
